      "message": "feat(browser-compute): B7-PRE1 identity envelope + durable effect ledger + action-plane seam closure\n\nDeep research (research/A2_METAENGINE_BROWSER_ARCHITECTURE_DEEP_RESEARCH_2026-08-29.md)\nverified the actual multi-head state (shell afc5554 / extension 09a205a6 /\ncompute 3eccaee / main 0d1c074c) and ranked amplifiers; the strongest minimal\nslice ships here:\n\n- browser-shared/effect-ledger.mjs: identity envelope v1 + hash-chained\n  append-only effect event contract (6 types, canonical JSON, full-chain\n  verification incl. tail-truncation against the persisted head)\n- src/effect-ledger-store.mjs: per-profile store, atomic writes, chain\n  verified on load, appends fail closed on a broken chain\n- action-kernel: INTENT_SEALED chained BEFORE CDP dispatch (second\n  pre-effect fence), EFFECT_OBSERVED, RECEIPT_EMITTED with receipt digest;\n  every event carries the full identity envelope; ledger-optional back-compat\n- runtime: navigate/click/type/submit actions now exist on the real runtime\n  and route exclusively through the ActionKernel — closes the B5->B6 seam\n  where dispatchRpc targeted nonexistent runtime methods; ledger.head/\n  verify/timeline evidence surface; runtime 0.3.0-dev.4\n- rpc-server + protocol-v1.json 1.4.0: three READ_ONLY ledger methods with\n  strict param allowlists\n\nTests: 121/121 (102 prior + 12 ledger + 7 seam), parse gate clean. B6\ninvariants untouched; ledger is evidence, never authority.",
